# Exclude the CONTENTS, not the directory itself: git never descends into an
# excluded directory, so a negation inside one can never re-include anything.
docs/marketing/*
# ...except the SEO blog. Its 22 sources and 208 built pages are already tracked,
# and web-deploy.yml copies docs/marketing/seo/site/blog into the apex tree, so a
# NEW article has to be committable too.
!docs/marketing/seo/
# ...and the landing, for the same reason one step further out. The apex
# sitemap.xml and llms-full.txt are emitted by build_landing.py, and those are
# what ai-budget.pl actually serves, so publishing an article has to commit
# them too. All 101 files here were already tracked; without this negation
# `git add docs/marketing/landing/...` is refused for the directory, which is
# how article 22 shipped with a sitemap that did not list it.
!docs/marketing/landing/
# Superpowers brainstorm artifacts
.superpowers/

